# Never commit model weights or captures (use GitHub Releases + SHA-256 in README)
weights/
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.pt
*.pth
*.keras

# Raw dataset downloads and derived artifacts
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
artifacts/
results/

# The DEMO artifact lane (scripts/bootstrap_demo_artifacts.py). Ignored, and the
# case is close enough to be worth writing down.
#
# FOR COMMITTING IT: the whole problem this lane solves is that a judge clones
# the repository and cannot run anything. A lane that only exists after someone
# runs a script they were never told about solves that problem only for people
# who read scripts/. Committing it would make the app work on a bare clone with
# no step in between, and the capture the weights are fitted from is committed
# already, so nothing unreproducible enters the tree.
#
# AGAINST, and this is what wins: CLAUDE.md forbids committing weights, and the
# exception it grants is for the synthetic pcap, not for models fitted from it.
# More concretely — committed demo weights would be the ONLY model files in the
# tree, in a repository whose README quotes AUROC figures measured on a model
# that is not here. `demo_engine_model.json` sitting in git, with a README
# reporting 0.933, is precisely the confusion the rest of this lane's design
# exists to prevent, and no amount of naming fixes a file that is simply there.
#
# THE NUMBERS, RE-MEASURED THIS SESSION, because the version of this note that
# was inherited had both of them wrong and they pointed the wrong way. It said
# "nine committed files (~200 KB, measured)". The built lane is TWELVE files and
# 1,090,206 bytes — 1.04 MiB, five times the figure quoted — because eight
# XGBoost head files of ~135 KB each dominate it, not the small JSON. And the
# cost of NOT committing it is one command, timed twice here at 15.2 s and
# 17.3 s (`python scripts/bootstrap_demo_artifacts.py`, wall clock, on a machine
# shared with other work), not the 44.7 s that was written down. So the trade is
# "1 MiB of model files in git, forever, in a repository that must not contain
# model files" against "about fifteen seconds, once". Both corrections make the
# case for ignoring it stronger than the note claimed.
#
# That command must therefore be put in front of the judge rather than left to
# be discovered — in README.md and docs/INSTALL.md, both of which belong to the
# orchestrator (see needs_orchestrator). If it does not appear there, this
# decision is wrong and the lane should be committed instead.
artifacts_demo/

# Offline wheel-house (rebuilt by scripts/build_vendor.ps1; too large for git)
vendor/*.whl
vendor/*.tar.gz

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated engine output (ledger, checkpoints, forecasts) — never committed
run/
# Local Claude Code settings (launch.json is kept; personal settings are not)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Anonymisation key (never committed — CLAUDE.md); set SIH26_HMAC_KEY from here
.env

# The synthetic demo capture IS bundled (small, deterministic, illustrative —
# regenerable via `python -m capture.make_synthetic_demo`). NOT real capture data.
!app/assets/synthetic_demo.pcap

# Diagnostic data caches (regenerable; the committed evidence is the .png/.json)
diagnostics/*.npz
